  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual\">Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual</a></i> </p><p>The process of crafting a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Synthetic_Lightsaber_Crystal\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Synthetic Lightsaber Crystal\">Synthetic Lightsaber Crystal</a> attempts to replicate millennia of geological compression and crystallization using machines and computers, which sometimes can fail. On occasion, the crystal's structure comes out far more compressed than a standard <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsaber_Crystal\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Lightsaber Crystal\">Lightsaber Crystal</a>. Compressed Crystals function perfectly well as <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsaber_Crystals\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Lightsaber Crystals\">Lightsaber Crystals</a>, producing a blade that is far thinner and more precise than the standard <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsaber_Crystal\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Lightsaber Crystal\">Lightsaber Crystal</a>. When you are attuned to a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsaber\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Lightsaber\">Lightsaber</a> with a Compressed Crystal, the targets of your <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsaber\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Lightsaber\">Lightsaber</a> attacks take a -2 penalty on <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Use_the_Force\" title=\"Use the Force\">Use the Force</a> checks made to negate the attack with the <b><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Block\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Block\">Block</a></b> Talent. </p>",
